/-!
# Finite type across `𝓕 ↦ 𝓕^a`, in the sense of Modules on Sites, Definition 03DL (5)

Let `S` be a scheme and `𝓕` a quasi-coherent `𝒪_S`-module.  Descent, Lemma 05VG says that the
equivalences `QCoh(𝒪_S) ⟶ QCoh((Sch/S)_τ, 𝒪)` and `QCoh(𝒪_S) ⟶ QCoh(S_τ, 𝒪)`, `𝓕 ↦ 𝓕^a`,
of Descent, Proposition 03DX preserve and reflect the properties of modules of Modules on Sites,
Definitions 03DE, 03DL and 03ER.  For the property "finite type", Definition 03DL (5), this
reads: `𝓕` is of finite type if and only if `𝓕^a` is of finite type as an `𝒪`-module.

Definition 03DL (5) on a ringed site `(𝒞, 𝒪)`: a sheaf of `𝒪`-modules `𝓖` is of finite type if
every object `U` of `𝒞` has a covering `{Uᵢ ⟶ U}` such that each restriction `𝓖|_{𝒞/Uᵢ}` is
generated by finitely many global sections.  This is `SheafOfModules.IsFiniteTypeOnSite`, and it
is the predicate used on both sides below: on the left for `𝓕` on the site of opens of `S` with
the structure sheaf `𝒪_S`, and on the right for `𝓕^a` on the site in question.

The ten cases of the lemma for this property, one theorem each:

* `(Sch/S)_Zar`: `AlgebraicGeometry.Cells05VG.isFiniteTypeOnSite_iff_baseAssociatedModule_zariski`
* `(Sch/S)_étale`: `AlgebraicGeometry.Cells05VG.isFiniteTypeOnSite_iff_baseAssociatedModule_etale`
* `(Sch/S)_smooth`:
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Cells05VG.isFiniteTypeOnSite_iff_baseAssociatedModule_smooth`
* `(Sch/S)_syntomic`:
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Cells05VG.isFiniteTypeOnSite_iff_baseAssociatedModule_syntomic`
* `(Sch/S)_fppf`: `AlgebraicGeometry.Cells05VG.isFiniteTypeOnSite_iff_baseAssociatedModule_fppf`
* `S_Zar`: `AlgebraicGeometry.Cells05VG.isFiniteTypeOnSite_iff_smallZariskiAssociatedModule`
* `S_étale`: `AlgebraicGeometry.Cells05VG.isFiniteTypeOnSite_iff_smallEtaleAssociatedModule`
* `S_smooth`:
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Cells05VG.isFiniteTypeOnSite_iff_smallFlatSiteAssociatedModule_smooth`
* `S_syntomic`:
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Cells05VG.isFiniteTypeOnSite_iff_smallFlatSiteAssociatedModule_syntomic`
* `S_fppf`: `AlgebraicGeometry.Cells05VG.isFiniteTypeOnSite_iff_smallFlatSiteAssociatedModule_fppf`

The functors are those of Proposition 03DX: `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.baseAssociatedModule`
on the big sites, `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallZariski.associatedModule`,
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.associatedModule`, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallFlatSite.associatedModule` on the small sites.

## Main results

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFiniteTypeOnSite_iff_isFiniteType`: on any site, Definition 03DL (5)
  agrees with Mathlib's `SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType`, which asks for one family covering the
  final object on whose members the module admits finitely many generating sections.
* The ten theorems listed above.

## Implementation notes

Each case is the corresponding statement for Mathlib's `SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType`, read on
both sides through `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFiniteTypeOnSite_iff_isFiniteType`.

Quasi-coherence of `𝓕` is the hypothesis of the source, which states the lemma for the
equivalences on quasi-coherent modules.  On `S_Zar` and on `S_étale` neither implication uses
it, so those two statements are made for every `𝒪_S`-module.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 05VG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05VG)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DL)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory

universe u v w

namespace Stacks.SheafOfModules

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{w}}
  [∀ X : C, HasSheafify (J.over X) AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
  [∀ X : C, (J.over X).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]

/-- **Modules on Sites, Definition 03DL (5), in its two forms.**  A sheaf of modules satisfies
`SheafOfModules.IsFiniteTypeOnSite` (every object has a covering on whose members the module is
generated by finitely many global sections) if and only if it is of finite type in Mathlib's
sense (one family covering the final object, with finitely many generating sections on each
member). -/
theorem isFiniteTypeOnSite_iff_isFiniteType (M : _root_.SheafOfModules.{w} R) :
    M.IsFiniteTypeOnSite ↔ M.IsFiniteType :=
  ⟨isFiniteType_of_isFiniteTypeOnSite M, isFiniteTypeOnSite_of_isFiniteType M⟩

end Stacks.SheafOfModules

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Cells05VG

open Stacks.SheafOfModules (isFiniteTypeOnSite_iff_isFiniteType)

section Big

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)

/-- **Descent, Lemma 05VG, finite type (03DL (5)), on the big site `(Sch/S)_Zar`.**  A
quasi-coherent `𝒪_S`-module `𝓕` is of finite type if and only if `𝓕^a` is of finite type as an
`𝒪`-module on `(Sch/S)_Zar`. -/
@[stacks 05VG "finite type, big site (Sch/S)_Zar"]
theorem isFiniteTypeOnSite_iff_baseAssociatedModule_zariski (𝓕 : S.Modules)
    [𝓕.IsQuasicoherent] :
    SheafOfModules.IsFiniteTypeOnSite (R := S.ringCatSheaf) 𝓕 ↔
      ((BigFppfOver.baseAssociatedModule B S hS .zariski).obj 𝓕).IsFiniteTypeOnSite :=
  (isFiniteTypeOnSite_iff_isFiniteType (R := S.ringCatSheaf) 𝓕).trans
    ((BigFppfOver.isFiniteType_baseAssociatedModule_iff B S hS .zariski 𝓕).trans
      (isFiniteTypeOnSite_iff_isFiniteType _).symm)

/-- **Descent, Lemma 05VG, finite type (03DL (5)), on the big site `(Sch/S)_étale`.**  A
quasi-coherent `𝒪_S`-module `𝓕` is of finite type if and only if `𝓕^a` is of finite type as an
`𝒪`-module on `(Sch/S)_étale`. -/
